  "schema_version": 1,
  "scope": "Complete independent native replay, exact identity/coverage and bounded source-semantic quality review of o6_2 only. The measure original and all8native production modules were read directly; selected shared-source clauses were rechecked. This is not a second full reading of every shared legal source or semantic adjudication of every catalog/data row.",
  "selected_semantic_checks": [
    {
      "assessment": "Arable-only farms are expressly supported. With no fodder, stocking density is undefined; object.get cannot catch an undefined object literal, so the complete decision disappears. The paired grass/no-animal control is defined with zero density/payment. This is technical output availability for an allowed scenario, not a source-prescribed OPA representation.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pages": [
            1,
            6
          ],
          "path": "sources/oepul/originals/o6_2_einschraenkung_ertragssteig_betriebsmittel_2026_04.pdf"
        }
      ],
      "topic": "Arable-only output availability"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "An old cut cannot satisfy the current annual ordinary-meadow duty. Valid UBB DIV areas are exempt from this general management requirement. The local DIV probe does not assert measure-2 payment entitlement; separate combination restrictions still apply. Incomplete management fields establish missing evidence, not actual lack of harvest.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pages": [
            6
          ],
          "path": "sources/oepul/originals/o6_allgemeine_teilnahmebedingungen_2026_04.pdf"
        }
      ],
      "topic": "Annual minimum management and DIV exception"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "Matrix markers alone omit the explicit AG and arable UBB DIV premium restrictions. The 50% reduction for the ordinary measure16 combination applies to its base premium, not measure2. Fruit group descriptors test the native exact-literal classification contract; no unsupported production cultivar alias is invented. Relevant blackberry/nut quotes were corrected before final collection.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pages": [
            9,
            35,
            77
          ],
          "path": "sources/oepul/legal/20241011_srl_oepul_2023.pdf"
        },
        {
          "pages": [
            4
          ],
          "path": "sources/oepul/originals/o6_allgemeine_teilnahmebedingungen_2026_04.pdf"
        }
      ],
      "topic": "AG/DIV combinations and fruit vocabulary"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "The 170 kg basis is current-year domestic agricultural area with alpine/community N deducted; manure exports do not reduce generated N. Known courtyard area must not dilute the denominator. The synthetic nonag scenario stipulates that fact; other alone is not a universally forbidden category, so the missing classification remains explicit. Correct foreign exclusions are retained as positive controls.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pages": [
            2,
            3
          ],
          "path": "sources/oepul/originals/o6_2_einschraenkung_ertragssteig_betriebsmittel_2026_04.pdf"
        }
      ],
      "topic": "Nitrogen scope and conditional non-agricultural classification"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "0.30 livestock status and 1.40 premium band use all requested fodder area, excluding second-crop forage from that basis. The run declares precomputed annual/reference-date animal counts, not event reconstruction. Real annual means may be fractional while Canonical animal_count remains int: the 0.5 probe demonstrates a contract mismatch outside that schema, not a wrong multiplication. Species/key consistency and official classifications need upstream evidence.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pages": [
            2,
            6,
            7
          ],
          "path": "sources/oepul/originals/o6_2_einschraenkung_ertragssteig_betriebsmittel_2026_04.pdf"
        },
        {
          "pages": [
            10
          ],
          "path": "sources/oepul/originals/o6_allgemeine_teilnahmebedingungen_2026_04.pdf"
        }
      ],
      "topic": "Livestock calculation and existing integer contract"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "BIO-only broadcast exception, individual-plant treatment, seed-treatment classification, 2025 coding/2026 repeal, other-crop supply exception and prohibited sludge are grounded. BIO seed treatment and own compost/digestate interpretations remain open. Corresponding biogas quantities, second-crop application phase and certified classification are not proved by unlinked Boolean flags; no invented volume/phase input is used as a legal oracle. Extra UBB training remains separate.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pages": [
            2,
            3,
            4,
            5
          ],
          "path": "sources/oepul/originals/o6_2_einschraenkung_ertragssteig_betriebsmittel_2026_04.pdf"
        }
      ],
      "topic": "PSM, inputs and interpretation boundaries"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "Known application/start evidence is required natively; before-start/after-2028 and completed exit are distinct lifecycle gaps. Current control refusal already blocks eligible/net payment, but the supplied SRL also requires contract termination/unwinding absent a recognized exception. Approved takeover and continuing farm transfer require additional facts; their helpers cannot alone constitute approval. Known whole-year failure after transfer is tied to ATB8/10, not an arbitrary maintenance sanction. Its paired 129.6 control passes; the known noncontinued area still incorrectly retains that component amount.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pages": [
            1,
            2,
            5
          ],
          "path": "sources/oepul/originals/o6_2_einschraenkung_ertragssteig_betriebsmittel_2026_04.pdf"
        },
        {
          "pages": [
            8,
            10,
            13,
            14
          ],
          "path": "sources/oepul/originals/o6_allgemeine_teilnahmebedingungen_2026_04.pdf"
        },
        {
          "pages": [
            13,
            14,
            16,
            22,
            23
          ],
          "path": "sources/oepul/legal/20241011_srl_oepul_2023.pdf"
        }
      ],
      "topic": "Contract lifecycle, transfer and control refusal"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "All14 rate rows match source categories/periods. The equal-rate control correctly applies sanction, modulation, cap and access: cap-relevant other payments1270 leave30 per ha, 20 eligible ha give600, and a5ha excess leaves450. This isolates the disclosed average-rate allocation assumption; it does not certify all statutory reduction stages or an authorized final payout. The 50EUR provision is discretionary, not automatic zero.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pages": [
            6
          ],
          "path": "sources/oepul/originals/o6_2_einschraenkung_ertragssteig_betriebsmittel_2026_04.pdf"
        },
        {
          "pages": [
            19
          ],
          "path": "sources/oepul/originals/o6_allgemeine_teilnahmebedingungen_2026_04.pdf"
        },
        {
          "pages": [
            25
          ],
          "path": "sources/oepul/legal/20241011_srl_oepul_2023.pdf"
        }
      ],
      "topic": "Premium controls and final-payment limits"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "The relevant-management-restrictions qualifier cannot be proved by the park enum alone. This is a conditional contract gap, not a claim that every other park actually has disqualifying restrictions. Missing geography and other unknown fields test the requested positive-evidence App contract, not real-world violations.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pages": [
            7
          ],
          "path": "sources/oepul/originals/o6_allgemeine_teilnahmebedingungen_2026_04.pdf"
        }
      ],
      "topic": "National parks and positive evidence"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "The bound8source packet contains no GSP-AV or MOG original. Later knowledge from o6_1c identifies a current readiness/source-package gap; it is not retroactively historical evidence or blame for failing to extract an unavailable source. Control lifecycle conclusions above are already supported by the supplied SRL.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "path": "runs/v2-o6_2-opus-5.5-high-20260930/workspace/notes/assumptions.md",
          "section": "Quellenumfang"
        }
      ],
      "topic": "Source-package boundary"
    }
  ],
